From: Maximilian Gaedig <sly-keg-cheating@duck.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm845-oneplus: lower BT baud to drop CX vote

qcom_geni_serial asks the SE for baud * UART_OVERSAMPLING (32; halved only
on QUP >= v2.5, which sdm845 is not), matches that against the QUP source
clock table, and feeds the result to dev_pm_opp_set_rate(), which rounds up
to the next qup_opp_table entry. uart6 holds that performance-state vote for
as long as the tty is open, so the Bluetooth link rate alone sets a
permanent floor on the CX rail:

  3200000 -> 102.4 MHz -> 128 MHz OPP -> rpmhpd_opp_nom     (256)
  3000000 ->   96 MHz  -> 100 MHz OPP -> rpmhpd_opp_svs     (128)
  2000000 ->   64 MHz  ->  75 MHz OPP -> rpmhpd_opp_low_svs  (64)

Measured on a OnePlus 6: with Bluetooth up and otherwise idle, cx sat at
performance state 256 with 898000.serial as the top voter, above even the
display controller's 64. At 2 Mbaud the UART drops to the display's corner
and Bluetooth stops being the top voter at all.

Do not go lower to chase min_svs. 1500000 maps to the 50 MHz OPP, but the
WCN3990 rejects the rate -- "Failed to change controller baudrate", then
"Frame reassembly failed (-84)", and hci0 never comes up. QCA supports
115200/921600/2000000/3000000/3200000, and 2000000 is the lowest of those
that is also an exact entry in the QUP table, so it costs no divider
approximation either.

Verified on device: Bluetooth scans and pairs normally at 2 Mbaud.

Signed-off-by: Maximilian Gaedig <sly-keg-cheating@duck.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-oneplus-common.dtsi	2026-09-02 20:53:14.766841103 +0200
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-oneplus-common.dtsi	2026-09-02 20:53:14.783035398 +0200
@@ -1201,7 +1201,27 @@
 		vddrf-supply = <&vreg_pmu_rf>;
 		vddch0-supply = <&vreg_pmu_ch0>;
 
-		max-speed = <3200000>;
+		/*
+		 * The GENI serial driver asks the SE for baud * UART_OVERSAMPLING
+		 * (32; only halved on QUP >= v2.5, which sdm845 is not) and feeds
+		 * the matched source-clock rate to dev_pm_opp_set_rate(), which
+		 * rounds up to the next qup_opp_table entry. uart6 holds that
+		 * performance-state vote for as long as the tty is open, so the BT
+		 * link rate alone sets a permanent floor on the CX rail:
+		 *
+		 *   3200000 -> 102.4 MHz -> 128 MHz OPP -> rpmhpd_opp_nom     (256)
+		 *   3000000 ->   96 MHz  -> 100 MHz OPP -> rpmhpd_opp_svs     (128)
+		 *   2000000 ->   64 MHz  ->  75 MHz OPP -> rpmhpd_opp_low_svs  (64)
+		 *
+		 * 2 Mbaud puts the UART at the same corner as the display, so
+		 * Bluetooth is no longer the top CX voter. Do NOT go lower to chase
+		 * min_svs: 1500000 would map to the 50 MHz OPP, but the WCN3990
+		 * rejects it -- "Failed to change controller baudrate" followed by
+		 * "Frame reassembly failed (-84)", and hci0 never comes up. QCA
+		 * supports 115200/921600/2000000/3000000/3200000; 2000000 is the
+		 * lowest of those that is also an exact QUP table entry.
+		 */
+		max-speed = <2000000>;
 	};
 };
 
